Subject: methRead no longer deleting uncompressed files after tabix compression
Message-ID: <pE9eAMD_wr4.EIMGD_p8DQAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/pE9eAMD_wr4/m/EIMGD_p8DQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi methylKit team! Quick question - I recently moved to the newest version of R and the most recent Bioconductor release of methylKit, and when running methRead on processBismarkAln output, the uncompressed .txt file is not deleted after the .bgz and index files are created. As far as I can tell no data is lost in the newly created databases. This is unexpected as during my previous work using version 1.8.1, the .txts were deleted; I wanted to confirm if this is expected behavior.

This can be replicated by using the vignette code as below:

file.list=list( system.file("extdata", "test1.myCpG.txt", package = "methylKit"), system.file("extdata", "test2.myCpG.txt", package = "methylKit"), system.file("extdata", "control1.myCpG.txt", package = "methylKit"), system.file("extdata", "control2.myCpG.txt", package = "methylKit") ) # read the files to a methylRawListDB object: myobjDB # and save in databases in folder methylDB myobjDB=methRead(file.list, sample.id <http://sample.id>=list("test1","test2","ctrl1","ctrl2"), assembly="hg18", treatment=c(1,1,0,0), context="CpG", dbtype = "tabix", dbdir = "methylDB" )

Thanks!!
Nia

